waive -du {  {CLK_GATE}  }  -msg {Latch inferred for signal 'Latch_Out' in module 'CLK_GATE'}  -rule {  {InferLatch}  }  -comment {Rule: InferLatch Location: CLK_GATE.v (Latch_Out) Status: Waived  Intentional Justification: The inferred latch is a deliberate Integrated Clock Gating (ICG) cell implementation, not an unintended combinational latch. The latch captures CLK_EN while CLK is low and holds it stable throughout the high phase of the clock, ensuring GATED_CLK = CLK && Latch_Out is generated glitch-free. This is the standard RTL coding pattern for clock gating prior to synthesis mapping onto a technology-specific ICG cell (e.g., TLATNCAX12M per the commented instantiation). Removing the latch (e.g., replacing with plain combinational logic) would introduce glitch risk on the gated clock and is explicitly avoided. Action Required: Confirm synthesis clock-gating inference (set_clock_gating_style -positive_edge_logic integrated) correctly maps this construct onto a library ICG cell rather than retaining a literal latch in the final netlist. No RTL change required.}  -exact 
waive -du {  {CLK_GATE}  }  -msg {Latch inferred for signal 'Latch_Out' in module 'CLK_GATE'}  -rule {  {InferLatch}  }  -comment {Rule: InferLatch Location: CLK_GATE.v (Latch_Out) Status: Waived  Intentional Justification: The inferred latch is a deliberate Integrated Clock Gating (ICG) cell implementation, not an unintended combinational latch. The latch captures CLK_EN while CLK is low and holds it stable throughout the high phase of the clock, ensuring GATED_CLK = CLK && Latch_Out is generated glitch-free. This is the standard RTL coding pattern for clock gating prior to synthesis mapping onto a technology-specific ICG cell (e.g., TLATNCAX12M per the commented instantiation). Removing the latch (e.g., replacing with plain combinational logic) would introduce glitch risk on the gated clock and is explicitly avoided. Action Required: Confirm synthesis clock-gating inference (set_clock_gating_style -positive_edge_logic integrated) correctly maps this construct onto a library ICG cell rather than retaining a literal latch in the final netlist. No RTL change required.}  -exact 
waive -rule {  {STARC05-1.4.3.4}  }  -comment {Rule: STARC05-1.4.3.4  Flip-flop clock signals must not be used as non-clock signals Location: ClkDiv.v (clk_div / div_clk used in o_div_clk combinational mux) Status: Waived  Intentional Justification: clk_div is a generated (internally divided) clock, classified as a clock net by the linter because it downstream drives clock ports (CLK_RX/CLK_TX). Within the divider module, it is legitimately combined through synchronous reset logic and a combinational selector (clk_en ? div_clk : i_ref_clk) to implement the ratio-based division and reference-clock bypass path. This is the standard RTL construct for a clock-divider/clock-mux block and is inherent to its function; the flagged usage does not indicate a design defect. Action Required: None. No RTL change required.} 
waive -rule {  {STARC05-1.4.3.4}  }  -comment {Rule: STARC05-1.4.3.4  Flip-flop clock signals must not be used as non-clock signals Location: ClkDiv.v (clk_div / div_clk used in o_div_clk combinational mux) Status: Waived  Intentional Justification: clk_div is a generated (internally divided) clock, classified as a clock net by the linter because it downstream drives clock ports (CLK_RX/CLK_TX). Within the divider module, it is legitimately combined through synchronous reset logic and a combinational selector (clk_en ? div_clk : i_ref_clk) to implement the ratio-based division and reference-clock bypass path. This is the standard RTL construct for a clock-divider/clock-mux block and is inherent to its function; the flagged usage does not indicate a design defect. Action Required: None. No RTL change required.} 